# pi - Pi via the LiteLLM proxy on Gemini 3.5 Flash (cheap default for simple,
#      high-volume tasks; saves cost vs. Pro). Shadows the `pi` binary so plain
#      `pi` routes through the proxy and is cost-tracked by the prefix+u popup.
#      For the raw, un-proxied agent use `command pi`.
#
#      Thin wrapper over `piv`, which owns the proxy guard and the per-pane cost
#      marker; only the model differs (set via $PI_LITELLM_MODEL). See `piv` for
#      proxy/auth details.
#
#   pi [pi-args...]   Run Pi against gemini-3.5-flash via LiteLLM.
#   pires             Resume such a session (pi --resume).
piv "$@"
